```js
let serviceFeeRate = 0.05;

export function setServiceFeeRate(rate) {
  serviceFeeRate = rate;
}

export function totalWithFee(subtotalCents) {
  return Math.round(subtotalCents * (1 + serviceFeeRate));
}
```

A teammate says this is fine because "the rate only changes once, at start-up". Explain the concrete problems this design creates and what you would change. Give at least one problem that is not about testing.

```js
if (score < 40) return 'fail';
else if (score > 40 && score < 70) return 'pass';
else if (score >= 70) return 'merit';
return 'unknown';
```

Which input reaches `'unknown'`, and what does that tell you about the specification?

```js
function makeLabels(names) {
  const out = [];
  for (let k = 0; k < names.length; k += 1) {
    out.push(function () { return names[k]; });
  }
  return out;
}
```

What does `makeLabels(['a','b'])[0]()` return, and what would it return if `let k` were `var k`?
